From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomtomnet <tompere8000@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:21:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ui/sdl2: share the clipboard with the guest

The SDL display had no clipboard peer, unlike the GTK, VNC and D-Bus
displays, so with qemu-vdagent,clipboard=on no text went between the
host clipboard and the guest.

Host copies are announced to the guest, which asks for the text when
something pastes it there.  Guest copies are fetched right away and put
in the host clipboard, since SDL 2 only takes the text itself.  Text is
compared with what was last exchanged, so that nothing goes back where
it came from, and so that Wayland reporting the clipboard again at each
focus change does not take the clipboard back from the guest.  When a
guest agent connects (qemu-vdagent resets the clipboard serials then),
the host clipboard is offered to it again.

On Wayland, SDL sets the clipboard only with the serial of a key or
button press: without one it silently keeps the text to itself and
stops seeing the host clipboard.  So there guest text waits for a key
or button press in the focused window, which copying in the guest
usually is.

Tested with a fake guest agent under KWin, Hyprland and niri, with SDL
on Wayland and on X11.  -trace 'sdl2_clipboard*' shows what happens.

Local patch, not for upstream submission: QEMU does not accept
AI-generated code (docs/devel/code-provenance.rst).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
